# nvn/pso: the prewarm tail goes on from where an earlier session left the seed list (pso_tail.tsv), and its seed rows wait while the device is hot (DM_PSO_TAIL_RESUME, DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT)
#
# Origin:  written in this repository after the Ocarina of Time (Switch 2) device session of 2026-11-20 (iPhone 15 Pro). No upstream commit. Applies after 0414 (patch -p1 --forward,
#          no fuzz); it needs 0413 for "this device's rows" (pso_user.tsv first). paches/0007, 0008, 0009 still apply on top and land where they did.
# Licence: the licence of the tree it patches (the engine's MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds and contributors).
#
# WHAT THE LOG SHOWS (0412's tail)
#   Session 1 (SIGTERM about 90 s in): "pipeline prewarm stopped: the process is ending (570 lines done)" = the head's 464 + 106 of the tail. Session 2: the tail started again
#   at the same task ("22727 tasks (24699 lines)"), redid session 1's rows and more in its first 60 s ("954 of 22727 tasks done ... after 60 s": the libraries already in Metal's
#   compile cache take 1-4 ms) and then compiled for 37 minutes, 5,506 tasks by the end of the log, one worker at utility QoS, while the session ran at thermal state 2 for its first
#   1,150 s and its draws waited 930 s for compiles of their own: the tail's compiles share the Metal compiler (4 concurrent compilations on this phone) and the heat with them.
#   The tail's rows of the seed list are speculative (rows this device never drew); with 0413 the device's own rows come first in the list, before the seed's.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES
#   * WarmTask records its list (src) and the line of its first row; warm_start notes which list is the seed (the pso_manifest.tsv beside the shader map; none under DM_PSO_MANIFEST).
#   * Resume (DM_PSO_TAIL_RESUME, default on): the line after the last seed task the tail built WHOLE (a render pair cut by a stop is not counted) is kept in pso_tail.tsv beside
#     pso_user.tsv, with the seed's size, modification time and the shader chain; written as a .tmp renamed over the file, every 60 s (with the progress line), when the tail ends
#     (the seed's end) and when it stops. The next start's tail leaves out the seed tasks before that line (the head before the first frame is unchanged, so are this device's rows) and
#     goes on from there; once the seed was walked to its end, the tail builds only this device's rows. Another seed list (size, time or chain) starts again. =0: walks them again.
#     A tail that left rows out ends with warm_finish_ex(0, 0): no archive sweep (Metal 4 path only), since those rows were not asked for in this run.
#   * Heat (DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT=1 turns it off): before each SEED task the tail reads NSProcessInfo.thermalState; at serious (2) or critical (3) it waits, looking again every 2 s,
#     and ends at once if the process or the graphics end meanwhile. This device's rows do not wait. The head, the draws' own compiles and the prefetch are not touched.
#   * DM_PSO_PREPARE_TAIL=user (new value; 0 and on as in 0412): the tail builds this device's rows only and none of the seed's, and keeps no position: what this device drew in
#     earlier sessions, built in the background, nothing speculative (for a game bound by memory, where the Memory saver profile sets DM_PSO_PREPARE_TAIL=0).
#   * Log: "pipeline prewarm tail: earlier sessions walked the seed list to its line L (pso_tail.tsv): K of the tail's N seed tasks are left out[, only this device's rows are built]",
#     "... the device is hot (thermal state T): the seed list's rows wait", "... cool again after S s", "finished ... (the seed tasks earlier sessions walked left out)",
#     "pipeline prewarm done (the seed rows earlier sessions walked were left out): ...".
#   Who owns the background work: the engine's tail runs only while the game runs (the app stops its own preparation at Play, BeginRun -> StopWarm: 0070 / 0076), and loads into the
#   process what the game is about to need (libraries and pipelines in memory, pipelines into 0414's archive); the app's preparation in iBuilder compiles libraries into Metal's compile
#   cache while no game runs. They never run at the same time; a library the app compiled is a cache hit (1-4 ms) for the tail.
#
# MEASURED on this Mac (M1 Pro): dm/gfx/tests t_pso_tail_resume, 40 checks, 0 failed, with DM_PSO_MTL4=0 and =1, on the GPU with t_pso_head's synthetic libraries (40 tasks, a head of
#   10): a tail stopped inside task 21 keeps the line after task 20; the next start leaves tasks 10..20 out and builds 21..39 (no sweep), keeps the end; the start after builds only the
#   head; DM_PSO_TAIL_RESUME=0 and a changed seed walk all again; at thermal state 2 (a test hook) this device's rows (25..39) are built and the seed's wait until cool, a stop while it
#   waits ends it, DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT=1 does not wait; DM_PSO_PREPARE_TAIL=user builds rows 25..39 (this device's) and no seed row. t_pso_head (348), t_pso_user_first (44), t_pso_warm,
#   t_pso_archive unchanged. Mutations (target/agent-work/eng/tools/mutate.py): a pair cut by a stop counted as walked fails 3 checks, no wait while hot fails 5.
#   dm/gfx/tests/t_pso_user_first.m (0413's test) now sets DM_PSO_TAIL_RESUME=0 and DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT=1: its second prepare run otherwise found the first
#   run's pso_tail.tsv and left its seed tasks out (2 of its 44 checks failed), and its tail would wait on a hot Mac.
# REVISION 2 (2026-11-21, after the read-only review target/agent-work/review-eng/REVIEW.txt, findings M2 (1), L3, L7):
#   * M2 (1): mtl_warm_pause(on), called first thing by dm_gfx_suspend (hle_nvn.c; a weak empty one there where nvn_mtl.m is not linked, the simulator host): while graphics are
#     suspended (the app in the background, app patch 0030) the tail finishes the task under way and takes no new one, so 0414's background write is not beside its compiles and the
#     process does no speculative work in the background; dm_gfx_suspend(0) lets it go on. Logged ("paused (graphics suspended ...)", "goes on (graphics resumed)").
#   * L3: the hot and paused waits look again every 250 ms (was 2 s), so a stop or dm_gfx_teardown waits at most that.
#   * L7: dm/host/dm_envflag.h (new, pure C: dm_flag_text, dm_env_flag, dm_flag_is): 1 / on / true / yes and 0 / off / false / no, any case, blanks allowed; anything else keeps the
#     default and is logged. Used here for DM_PSO_PREPARE_TAIL (0412's prepare_tail_on: "off" and "false" now turn the tail off as "0" did; "user" as before), DM_PSO_TAIL_RESUME and
#     DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT; engine-patches 0453, 0503 and 0504 include it for their own switches (so they need this patch before them, as the series has it).
#   MEASURED (this Mac): t_pso_tail_resume 55 checks, 0 failed, both compilers (the 40 before, plus: the pause holds the tail between two tasks and it goes on when resumed, a stop while
#   paused ends it in under a second, DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT=on does not wait, DM_PSO_PREPARE_TAIL=off skips the tail); t_env_flag 102 checks, 0 failed (every word, case, blank, bad value).
# NOT VERIFIED (iPhone only): the heat and frame-time effect of pausing at thermal state 2, whether the seed's rows left out are still in Metal's compile cache at a later session (it
#   keeps about 5,500-5,800 of this game's libraries, DEVICE-FINDINGS), how long a whole walk of the seed takes over sessions.
# RISKS: a row left out of the tail because an earlier session walked it, and evicted from Metal's cache since, is compiled when drawn (then it is in pso_user.tsv, so the next start
#   builds it first). A long hot spell leaves the seed's rows unbuilt in that session.
# Roll back: DM_PSO_TAIL_RESUME=0 and DM_PSO_TAIL_HOT=1 give 0412's tail back (=user is new: leave it unset); or remove this file from engine-patches/ and run scripts/build-host.sh again.

# REVISION 3 (2026-11-21, review L8, the trivial part): dm_gfx_teardown sets back the state of 0413's learned list and of this patch's tail seed (mtl_session_reset, after the background work is
